Yes—**react-native-maps** supports custom markers, and for a *mountain silhouette icon* the usual pattern is to use a local PNG/SVG image inside a `<Marker>`, or render custom child content inside the marker.[2][1]

A simple example with a mountain silhouette icon looks like this:

```tsx
import React from 'react';
import { View, Image, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';
import MapView, { Marker } from 'react-native-maps';

export default function App() {
  return (
    <MapView
      style={StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject}
      initialRegion={{
        latitude: 37.7749,
        longitude: -122.4194,
        latitudeDelta: 0.08,
        longitudeDelta: 0.08,
      }}
    >
      <Marker
        coordinate={{ latitude: 37.7749, longitude: -122.4194 }}
        title="Mountain Viewpoint"
        description="Scenic mountain location"
      >
        <Image
          source={require('./assets/mountain-silhouette.png')}
          style={styles.markerIcon}
          resizeMode="contain"
        />
      </Marker>
    </MapView>
  );
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  markerIcon: {
    width: 36,
    height: 36,
  },
});
```

This works because `react-native-maps` allows a marker to render an image asset as its icon, and it also supports custom children inside a marker that replace the default pin symbol.[2][1]

If you want a *true silhouette style* instead of a PNG, use an SVG-based approach or render a styled `View`/`Text` inside the marker; `react-native-maps` explicitly supports custom marker content, including native SVGs in the marker children.[2]

For multiple mountain markers, you can map over an array:

```tsx
const peaks = [
  { id: '1', latitude: 37.7749, longitude: -122.4194 },
  { id: '2', latitude: 37.7849, longitude: -122.4294 },
];

<MapView style={StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject} initialRegion={...}>
  {peaks.map((peak) => (
    <Marker
      key={peak.id}
      coordinate={{ latitude: peak.latitude, longitude: peak.longitude }}
    >
      <Image
        source={require('./assets/mountain-silhouette.png')}
        style={styles.markerIcon}
        resizeMode="contain"
      />
    </Marker>
  ))}
</MapView>
```

